  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EDUCATION EXTRACTIVES &amp; FINANCING 4 DEVT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resource Rights Africa  has capacity in advocating for the suitable use of natural resources including oil and gas, minerals, land,forests, water bodies as well as flora and fauna. Specifically under this project, Resources rights will contribute to impact area 2which is focused on ensuring that People experiencing poverty and most vulnerable to shocks, conflicts and crises are better able to claim and access their rights to well-being, peace and security.  the key activities tat RRA will implement include recruitment and training of human rights defenders within the mining communities on  human rights. this will continue to monitor and report human rights violations within their communities, Training of CSOs on the Extractive Industries Transparency Initiative (EITI) mechanism to strengthen their capacity on environmental monitoring, gender and extractive, revenue and tax tracking, and human rights. they will also target mining companies with an aim of making them understand their role in protecting the rights of people  as well as ensuring that they give back to the communities where they work. These among may other activities will lead to increased awareness and support for the rights of  women, youth and other vulnerable groups, and improved transparency and accountability of the private sector and government to the target communities</narrative>
  </description>
